{"text": "On the next market day, he went to Goderville only to tell his story, but Malandain laughed when he passed. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> A farmer did not even let him finish, but tapped him on the stomach and cried, Get along, you old rascal. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> At the inn, a horse dealer laughed and said that he knew all about that old trick with the string. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> But they found the pocketbook, stammered Hauchecorne, and the dealer replied, One man finds it, and another man returns it. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Suddenly he understood that people thought a partner had returned the money for him. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> He went home in shame and anger, for he knew that he was sly enough to play such a trick. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> If he had the chance, he would even boast of such a trick, and the whole town knew it. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> He made his story longer each day, but the more he explained, the less people believed him. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> He grew thinner and weaker, and jokers made him tell the story of the string just to laugh at him. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> He fell ill in December and died in January, repeating, A little piece of string, look, here it is, Mister Mayor.", "alignment": {"characters": ["O", "n", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "n", "e", "x", "t", " ", "m", "a", "r", "k", "e", "t", " ", "d", "a", "y", ",", " ", "h", "e", " ", "w", "e", "n", "t", " ", "t", "o", " ", "G", "o", "d", "e", "r", "v", "i", "l", "l", "e", " ", "o", "n", "l", "y", " ", "t", "o", " ", "t", "e", "l", "l", " ", "h", "i", "s", " ", "s", "t", "o", "r", "y", ",", " ", "b", "u", "t", " ", "M", "a", "l", "a", "n", "d", "a", "i", "n", " ", "l", "a", "u", "g", "h", "e", "d", " ", "w", "h", "e", "n", " ", "h", "e", " ", "p", "a", "s", "s", "e", "d", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "A", " ", "f", "a", "r", "m", "e", "r", " ", "d", "i", "d", " ", "n", "o", "t", " ", "e